#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1358
msgid "Oven Temperature for Baking: Celsius and Fahrenheit"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:379
msgid "Oven temperatures are not volumes—but they travel with recipes"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1411
msgid "Ovens vary. Rack position, pan colour, and calibration errors matter as much as the unit label. Use an oven thermometer."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1320
msgid "Packaging is often sold in boxes covering a stated area. Convert your net area (plus waste) into the seller’s unit before dividing by coverage per box. Round up to whole boxes."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:583
msgid "Paint coverage is area; paint purchase is volume. You need area of wall, number of coats, and coverage rate (m² per litre) to find litres. Converting wall m² directly into litres without coverage data is meaningless."
msgstr ""

#: src/lib/units.ts:1200
msgid "Parsec"
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:576
msgid "People confuse the words because everyday language is loose. We say a room is 20 squares, a pool holds 50 000 litres, and a field is 2 acres—then ask a converter to jump between those numbers without checking dimensions."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:510
msgid "Phone screens, notebooks, and desk accessories are marketed in inches in some regions even when the rest of life is metric. Treat those inches as marketing conventions and convert if you need clearance in a metric bag or sleeve."
msgstr ""

#: src/features/guides/data/guides.ts:1453
msgid "Pick one planning unit for the trip. Convert all legs into that unit. Add buffer for detours. Only then convert a summary into the local road-sign unit if needed."
msgstr ""

